Sharp the Cunning Man keeps a hut in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Deosil|Deosil]], a wooden shack on a hundred-foot patch of wet peat bog that the factories of the district were built up around. The ground outside his door stays goopy no matter the weather.

He is an old kobold, two and a half feet tall, blue-scaled, with a white-stained moustache and a long reptilian beard. The spikes along his spine have been ground down over the years. He wears a burlap tunic of the kind worn in rural, unconnected places, and has lived in this hut his whole life, burning incense in it since he was four. The one room is hung with tapestries, a few old and hand-woven and most cheap industrial work, all stained yellow with smoke. The entrance is a curtain of pebbles tied into twine. His floor is carved over with magic circles.

He works as a thaumaturge, a trade his father taught him and which he has practised for fifteen years. None of what he does follows the ordinary principles of magic; [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] read his work and could make no sense of the method, yet the results hold. He believes a thing should work, and through force of will and the blessing of the [[Iridescent Host|Host]] it does. His raiment marks him as blessed by the Host.

For two copper pieces he sold Anzu two ampoules of an oily yellow liquid, both made from crushed marble and olive oil, one for ulcers caused by coffee and one for ulcers caused by anxiety. He told Anzu to break the ampoule and breathe the vapour on the next new moon, and Anzu did, and the ulcers cleared. He carved a circle into his floor and filled the grooves with goat's blood to check the Party for fiendish influence, passing a censer over each of them and humming a pop song in a minor key. He found none of them possessed. He judged [[People/Johnny|Johnny]] and [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] tenuously settled in their own bodies. He asked [[People/Sir Arctos|Arctos]] for his autograph. He took the rest of Johnny's goat's blood as payment and told him to make blood sausage with it, then sent the Party out so he could hold a seance.
